# License

This repository uses a three-way license model, because it contains three
different kinds of work and one license does not fit all of them.

| Content | Paths | License | SPDX |
|---|---|---|---|
| Hardware design | `hardware/` | CERN Open Hardware Licence v2 — Strongly Reciprocal | `CERN-OHL-S-2.0` |
| Code | `esphome/`, `packages/`, `dashboards/`, `scripts/` | MIT | `MIT` |
| Documentation | `docs/`, `README.md` | Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International | `CC-BY-4.0` |

**Third-party files are not covered by any of the above.** Several vendor 3D
models and datasheets are redistributed here under their own terms, and one of
them is non-commercial. See **[THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)**
before you assume anything about reuse.

---

## Hardware: CERN-OHL-S v2

Everything under `hardware/` — the KiCad board, the gerbers and drill file, the
enclosure DXF — is licensed under the **CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2,
Strongly Reciprocal**. Full text: **[LICENSE-HARDWARE](LICENSE-HARDWARE)**.

You may study, modify, manufacture and sell boards based on this design. In
exchange, if you convey a modified design or a product made from it, you must
make the complete modified source available under the same license, and notify
recipients of where to get it.

The notice below applies to the hardware. If you modify the design, CERN-OHL-S
§3.3(b) requires you to add your own notice saying what you changed and when.

```
Copyright (C) 2026 William K. Collis

This source describes Open Hardware and is licensed under the CERN-OHL-S v2.

You may redistribute and modify this source and make products using it under
the terms of the CERN-OHL-S v2 (https://ohwr.org/cern_ohl_s_v2.txt).

This source is distributed WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTY, INCLUDING
OF MERCHANTABILITY, SATISFACTORY QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
Please see the CERN-OHL-S v2 for applicable conditions.

Source location: https://github.com/wkcollis1-eng/mmwave-presence-node
```

Third-party 3D models shipped alongside the board are **Available Components**
in the sense of CERN-OHL-S §1.7, and under §3.3(d) they remain licensed under
their own terms rather than this one.

